+Bootstrap renewal is separately negotiated through
+`GetCapabilities.supports_bootstrap_token_refresh`. When the gateway has a
+sandbox JWT issuer and the driver advertises this capability, the gateway
+mints a fresh token for the persisted sandbox ID and sends it in
+`StartSandboxRequest.sandbox_token`. Explicit starts, persisted `Starting`
+recovery, and running-intent startup use the same path under the lifecycle
+gate. Driver names are diagnostic and do not grant this capability. Older
+drivers receive an empty field. The signing key never leaves the gateway.
+
+The Docker driver advertises renewal. Before starting retained stopped compute,
+it verifies the exact managed container labels, stopped state, and read-only
+bootstrap bind mount. It atomically replaces only the existing owner-private
+token file and syncs it before Docker start. Unsafe, missing, or mismatched
+material fails closed. Running containers are unchanged. The configured token
+TTL and supervisor refresh policy remain unchanged, so shared gateways can
+retain positive expiry across stopped intervals longer than that TTL.
+
+An explicit authorized start may also retry a persisted `Error` when both
+bootstrap renewal and a gateway signer are present. The same lifecycle gate,
+identity checks and driver validation apply, and a failed retry retains the
+error. Automatic startup sweeps still exclude errors. This recovers retained
+containers that already failed bootstrap before renewal was installed.
+
