 For GPU-backed Docker sandboxes, configure Docker CDI before starting the gateway so OpenShell can detect the daemon capability.
 
+With gateway JWT signing enabled, retained starts renew the Docker supervisor's
+protected bootstrap token before starting the same stopped container. Files,
+caches, volumes, and the configured token TTL remain unchanged. This allows
+shared gateways to use a positive TTL even when a sandbox stays stopped past
+the original token's expiry. Already-running containers are unchanged. External
+drivers must advertise `supports_bootstrap_token_refresh` to receive fresh
+tokens; a driver name alone does not enable renewal.
+An explicit start can also recover an existing error under this signed renewal
+profile, including a container that failed bootstrap before the repair. Gateway
+startup does not automatically retry errors.
+
